    overview:
      "<p>The <strong>Gokyo Lake Trek</strong> follows a quieter branch of the Khumbu into one of the most photogenic corners of the Everest region. Leaving the main Base Camp trail above Namche Bazaar, the route climbs the Dudh Koshi valley through Dole and Machhermo to <strong>Gokyo (4,800 m)</strong>, a small settlement set beside a chain of brilliant turquoise glacial lakes at the edge of the <strong>Ngozumpa Glacier</strong>, the longest in the Himalaya.</p><p>The centrepiece of the trek is the climb to <strong>Gokyo Ri (5,357 m)</strong>, a viewpoint that takes in four of the world's six highest mountains — Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, and Cho Oyu — above the lakes and the glacier below. A morning walk to the fourth lake adds a further perspective on Cho Oyu's north face. With fewer trekkers than the Base Camp route, comfortable teahouses, and an acclimatization day in Namche, this 12-day itinerary is an excellent alternative for those who want high Khumbu scenery away from the crowds.</p>",
