          "<p><strong>Spring (March to May)</strong> and <strong>autumn (September to November)</strong> are the two seasons that make sense for Gokyo. Autumn is the classic window, with settled post-monsoon weather, exceptionally clear air, and the lakes at their most vividly blue. Spring is warmer, the days are longer, and rhododendron forest below Namche is in flower, though afternoon haze can build.</p><p>Winter is genuinely spectacular here — the lakes freeze and the light is superb — but nights at Gokyo drop below -20°C and a number of lodges close, so it is only worth considering with proper cold-weather gear. The monsoon (June to August) is not recommended: the mountains stay hidden, the trail from Dole upward becomes slippery, and Lukla flights are regularly grounded.</p>",
